ml-dev-kit adapts ideas and prompt wording from two MIT-licensed projects.

mattpocock/skills (https://github.com/mattpocock/skills)
Copyright (c) 2026 Matt Pocock
Adapted: the grilling and domain-modeling style (one decision at a time,
each with a recommended answer; CONTEXT.md and ADRs updated as decisions
settle), the TDD approach (agreed seams, one test then the code that passes
it), and the code-review axes (fidelity to the Spec judged apart from the
project's standards).

obra/superpowers (https://github.com/obra/superpowers)
Copyright (c) 2025 Jesse Vincent
Adapted: the subagent-driven-development structure (an implementer subagent
that reports its status, a separate reviewer that treats the report as
unverified claims, and a capped fix loop between them), and the builder
check that reads a spec cold before work starts.

